## Proposed Implementation Batch (Phase 7)

Given the audit, I recommend attacking **Tier 1 items 1–7** as a single coherent phase, since they form a natural cluster around:

1. **PM Command Center Intelligence** (items 1–3) — Makes the dashboard truly autonomous
2. **Auto-Translation** (item 4) — Completes the messaging triage story
3. **Dynamic Lease Term Pricing** (items 5–7) — The biggest unfulfilled feature cluster in rent-optimization

### Phase 7A: PM Command Center Intelligence

#### [NEW] `tenant_portal_backend/src/jobs/daily-action-items.service.ts`
- Cron job running at 6 AM scanning:
  - Leases expiring within 60 days without renewal offers
  - Maintenance tickets open >7 days
  - Tenants with >2 late payments in trailing 6 months
  - Units with occupancy gaps
- Emits `DAILY_ACTION_ITEM` intents with structured metadata

#### [MODIFY] `tenant_portal_backend/src/reporting/analytics.service.ts`
- Add `getPortfolioHealthHeatmap()` method computing per-property scores for: financial health (NOI margin), occupancy risk (vacancy rate), tenant sentiment (average sentiment score from messages)
- Add `getOpexAnomalies()` comparing current month vs trailing 12-month average

#### [NEW] `property_pulse/app/manager/dashboard/components/PortfolioHeatmap.tsx`
- Interactive grid visualization with color-coded health indicators per property
- Click-through to individual property drill-downs

#### [MODIFY] `property_pulse/app/manager/dashboard/page.tsx`
- Integrate heatmap component and OPEX anomaly alerts
- Handle `DAILY_ACTION_ITEM` intent rendering

---

### Phase 7B: Auto-Translation

#### [MODIFY] `tenant_portal_backend/src/messaging/sentiment-analysis.service.ts`
- Add `detectLanguage()` and `translateToEnglish()` methods (heuristic/pattern-based for common languages)
- Append `detectedLanguage` and `translatedContent` to message metadata

---

### Phase 7C: Dynamic Lease Term Pricing

#### [MODIFY] `tenant_portal_backend/src/rent-optimization/rent-optimization.service.ts`
- Add `generateSeasonalPricingMatrix(unitId, baseRent)` returning a 12-month pricing grid weighted by seasonal demand curves
- Add `generateRenewalOffers()` scanning leases expiring in 90 days

#### [NEW] `property_pulse/app/manager/rent-optimization/lease-pricing/page.tsx`
- Interactive slider/timeline UI where dragging the lease end-date updates the monthly rent
- Visual "savings" indicator for high-demand months

#### [MODIFY] `tenant_portal_backend/src/jobs/scheduled-jobs.service.ts`
- Add nightly cron for `generateRenewalOffers()` emitting `RENEWAL_PRICING_GENERATED` intents

---

## Proposed Implementation Batch (Phase 8)

Phase 8 picks up the remaining **Tier 1 items 8-15** and groups them into four backend-heavy delivery tracks:

1. **AI Prescreening Compliance + Risk Scoring** (items 8-11)
2. **Smart Escrow State Tracking** (item 12)
3. **Yield Sweeps / Rent Bifurcation** (item 13)
4. **Platform Governance & Sync Safeguards** (items 14-15)

This phase is intentionally less UI-heavy than Phase 7. The main complexity is in compliance, ledger correctness, auditability, and safe automation boundaries.

### Phase 8A: AI Prescreening Compliance + Tenancy Risk Scoring

#### [MODIFY] `tenant_portal_backend/src/rental-application/rental-application.ai.service.ts`
- Add `sanitizeForFairHousing()` to strip direct protected-class fields and redact obvious protected-class proxies from free text
- Add `computeTenancySuccessScore()` returning:
  - `score`
  - `decisionBand`
  - `decisionExplanation`
  - `traceabilityLog`
- Keep all scoring deterministic and explainable

#### [MODIFY] `tenant_portal_backend/src/rental-application/rental-application.service.ts`
- Invoke fair-housing sanitization before any risk scoring
- Attach traceability output to screening results and AI review metadata
- Emit `ApproveTenantIntent` when application score clears a configurable threshold
- Persist predicted score metadata for later calibration against actual outcomes

#### [MODIFY] `tenant_portal_backend/src/rental-application/dto/*`
- Extend DTOs only if needed to surface:
  - decision explanation
  - traceability log
  - predicted tenancy score

#### [FOLLOW-UP / PERSISTENCE] Rental outcome feedback loop
- Add or extend a persistence surface to record:
  - `applicationId`
  - `predictedScore`
  - `predictedBand`
  - `approvedAutomatically`
  - `actualOutcome`
  - delinquency / eviction / lease-completion markers
- This phase only records outcomes. It does not introduce retraining automation.

### Phase 8B: Smart Escrow State Tracking

#### [MODIFY] Billing / ledger services
- Introduce an escrow state machine with explicit states:
  - `FUNDED`
  - `HELD`
  - `DISPUTED`
  - `RELEASED`
- Associate escrow state changes with payment / deposit lifecycle events
- Ensure transitions are auditable and idempotent

#### [MODIFY] Relevant controllers and reporting surfaces
- Expose escrow status through existing billing or lease-related endpoints
- Add event history or ledger notes so operators can reconstruct the state path for any escrowed funds

### Phase 8C: Yield Sweeps / Rent Bifurcation

#### [MODIFY] Payment processing / post-payment flow
- Add a rent bifurcation rule engine for post-payment allocation:
  - management fee slice
  - reserve contribution
  - owner yield / disbursement
- Support property- or organization-level rule configuration
- Persist resulting split details in ledger-compatible metadata

#### [MODIFY] Payment webhook / posting logic
- Apply bifurcation after successful rent posting, not before funds are recognized
- Guard against double-splitting on webhook retries by using deterministic idempotency keys

### Phase 8D: Right to be Forgotten / GDPR Anonymization

#### [NEW] Privacy or compliance controller/service
- Add anonymization endpoint(s) for user data export and deletion workflows
- Support:
  - identify subject records
  - export relevant data snapshot
  - anonymize or delete personal data where permitted
- Keep legal / financial records intact where retention is required, but sever or redact personal identifiers

#### [MODIFY] Cross-module data services
- Define a consistent anonymization policy for:
  - users
  - messages
  - leases
  - payments
  - applications
  - audit metadata

### Phase 8E: Accounting Sync Anomaly Detection

#### [MODIFY] `tenant_portal_backend/src/quickbooks/*`
- Add anomaly detection around sync payloads and reconciliation output
- Detect mismatches such as:
  - duplicate invoice syncs
  - unexpected balance deltas
  - unusually large transaction variance
  - missing linked entities
- Emit operator-facing anomaly intents instead of silently failing or auto-correcting

#### [MODIFY] Dashboard / ops surfacing
- Reuse existing action-intent and admin monitoring surfaces where possible
- Provide enough metadata for operators to manually reconcile the anomaly

---

## Verification Plan

### Automated
- TypeScript compilation (`npx tsc --noEmit`) for both workspaces
- Verify cron registration in `app.module.ts`
- Check acceptance criteria boxes in user story docs
- Unit tests for:
  - fair-housing sanitization
  - tenancy success scoring
  - escrow state transitions
  - yield bifurcation calculations
  - anonymization redaction behavior
  - QuickBooks anomaly thresholds

### Manual
- Visual review of heatmap component in browser
- Verify intent rendering for new intent types on the dashboard
- Validate that auto-approval produces a traceable explanation and does not use protected-class inputs
- Walk an escrow item through each state transition
- Simulate a payment posting with yield sweep allocation rules
- Verify anonymized user records are no longer identifiable in operational UIs
- Simulate accounting sync anomalies and confirm they surface as operator-review events

## Open Questions

> [!NOTE]
> The remaining **18 mobile-native criteria** (Tier 3) are architecturally out of scope for our web stack and would require a separate React Native project. These should be deferred.
